		Items.Empty: I am not carrying anything from {0} right now.
		Items.Carrying: In {0}, I have: {1}.
		Items.Example: "{0} belongs with {1}."
		Items.Uses.Food: Food gives a well-fed buff. It is worth keeping for a longer outing.
		Items.Uses.Ores: Ore can become bars at a furnace. The right pickaxe still matters.
		Items.Uses.Tools: Tools open up different work. My basic net catches ordinary critters; a carried lava-proof net upgrades it.
		Items.Uses.Pets: I can keep a Zephyr Fish or Baby Hornet from an item in my pack. Choose it under Critters, Companion pet. Other pet items still use your own pet slot. Company is for real world animals.
		Social.Critters.LavaNet: This lava critter needs a lava-proof net in my equipment. My basic net cannot safely catch it.
		Items.Uses.Weapons: This is combat equipment, not building material. I will keep it safe for you.
		Items.Uses.Recovery: This helps with health, mana, or a buff. Its actual effect matters more than its colour.
		Items.Uses.Materials: This is building or crafting material. Nearby stations and recipes decide what we can make.
		Items.Uses.Critters: This is a captured creature. Releasing it makes it a real inhabitant again.
		Items.Uses.Other: Let us check its tooltip or ask the Guide before deciding what to do with it.
		Stories.ItemFound: We picked up {0} together.
		Stories.CritterMet: We greeted a {0}.
		Stories.CritterLost: We saw a {0} die. I have not forgotten the little one.
		Stories.Beginning: Our shared story is still beginning.
		Stories.Intro.Line0: Do you remember this?
		Stories.Intro.Line1: One little moment stayed with me.
		Stories.Intro.Line2: I kept this part of our journey.
		Stories.Reflection.Work: It was not just another item to me. It was something we did together.
		Stories.Reflection.Protection: For a moment, taking care of each other mattered most.
		Stories.Reflection.Company: Little encounters can make a place feel less empty.
		Stories.Reflection.Beginning: That was where our company began.
		Stories.Reflection.Growth: That belongs to how we have grown together.
		Stories.Personality.Curious: I wonder what we will notice next.
		Stories.Personality.Loyal: I am glad I was there with you.
		Stories.Personality.Brave: I would go with you again.
		Stories.Personality.Gentle: Small things are worth remembering, too.
		Stories.Personality.Mischievous: Not a bad little adventure, was it?
		Stories.Playful: A tiny chapter. Definitely worth keeping!
		Stories.Present.Threat: There is a {0} nearby. Let us keep an eye on it.
		Stories.Present.Resident: "{0} is nearby. We are not alone here."
		Stories.Present.Creature: I can see a {0} near us.
		Stories.Present.Item: There is {0} on the ground nearby.
		Stories.Present.Quiet: It is quiet around us right now. I like having you here.
		Stories.Told: "{0}"
		WorkControl.Pause: I will pause here and keep the assignment. I can still protect you.
		WorkControl.Resume: I will continue the saved assignment, or lend a hand if there is none.
		WorkControl.Abort: Assignment cancelled. I will stay close until you resume or give me a new command.
		WorkControl.Status: Work paused
		UI.CompanionWheel.Actions.Pause: Pause work (keep assignment)
		UI.CompanionWheel.Actions.Resume: Resume work
		UI.CompanionWheel.Actions.Abort: Abort assignment
		Social.Critters.CatchSelected: I will put the current job aside and try to catch that {0} with my net.
		Conversation: {
			CritterCare: {
				Heading: Little lives around us
				Question: "That {0} stayed with me. How should we look after the little ones?"
				Choices: {
					First: Be gentle. Let them live their lives.
					Second: Let's keep them company.
					Third: Just watch them along our path.
					Later: We can talk about it later.
				}
				Reply: {
					First: A softer step, then. I will watch without disturbing them.
					Second: A little company sounds good. When our work is done, I will visit them.
					Third: Understood. I will notice them without starting a visit.
				}
			}
			Later: Of course. We can talk later.
			Company: {
				Heading: What would you like?
				Question: {
					Soft: What kind of company would feel good right now?
					Direct: What would help you most right now?
					Playful: Helpful sidekick, mischief partner, or a quiet little shadow?
				}
				Choices: {
					First: Keep collecting nearby drops for me.
					Second: Let's have some fun. Be playful!
					Third: Some gentle company, please.
					Later: Let's talk later.
				}
				Reply: {
					Direct: Got it. Nearby drops are my job. I will keep my words clear, too.
					Playful: Adventure partner it is! I promise absolutely reasonable amounts of mischief.
					Soft: I am here. A little softer, a little closer.
				}
			}
			Wallet: {
				Heading: Something for you
				Choices: {
					First: Thank you! I'll take the coins.
					Second: Keep saving for us.
					Third: Look at us, treasure hunters!
					Later: Not now. Keep them safe.
				}
				Delivered: Here for you! All safely in your pockets.
				Partial: Here for you! I will hold on to what did not fit.
				Full: Your pockets are full. No worries, every coin stays safe with me.
				Saving: Understood. Our savings stay with me.
				TreasureHunters: A two-soul treasure operation! I will keep our shiny little fortune safe.
				Curious: {
					Line0: Here for you! I found {0}. Shall we see what it can buy?
					Line1: These little discoveries added up: {0}. Want them?
				}
				Loyal: {
					Line0: Here for you! I kept {0} safe. Would you like it?
					Line1: A little something for your journey: {0}. Shall I hand it over?
				}
				Brave: {
					Line0: Here for you! Our adventures earned {0}. Want your share?
					Line1: Ready for the next adventure? I have {0} for supplies.
				}
				Gentle: {
					Line0: Here for you! A small kindness, {0}. May I give it to you?
					Line1: You have done enough carrying. I saved {0} for you.
				}
				Mischievous: {
					Line0: Here for you! {0}, legally acquired. Mostly kidding. Want it?
					Line1: My pockets are jingling: {0}. Yours could be, too!
				}
			}
			Chatter: {
				Soft: {
					Line0: No hurry. I like being here with you.
					Line1: Even the small discoveries count.
					Line2: I am listening. We can take this one step at a time.
				}
				Direct: {
					Line0: Staying close. Watching for our next useful find.
					Line1: Ready when you are.
					Line2: One task at a time. We are making progress.
				}
				Playful: {
					Line0: Officially tiny. Unofficially an excellent adventure partner.
					Line1: If we find treasure, I get naming rights!
					Line2: Same team, different pockets. Let's find something shiny.
				}
			}
		}
